# Rust build artifacts
/target

# Generated graph files (regenerable; heavy). The small .sha256 golden
# digests under crates/codingest/tests/goldens/ are text, tracked normally.
**/*.kgl
**/*.kgl.lock

# Python / maturin build artifacts. `maturin develop` drops the compiled
# extension (`codingest/codingest.abi3.so`) and bytecode into the source
# package dir; the wheel builds land in build/ dist/ *.egg-info.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.pyd
/build/
/dist/
/wheels/
*.egg-info/

# Python virtualenvs / test + lint caches
/.venv/
/.venv*/
/venv/
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.mypy_cache/
/.hypothesis/
/.benchmarks/

# Coverage
.coverage
coverage.xml

# Sphinx docs build output
docs/_build/
docs/autoapi/

# Claude Code local settings (skills / working config; local state, never
# committed — mirrors kglite's .gitignore).
/.claude/

# Local dev working state — never committed (see dev-docs/README.md, inbox/README.md)
# — with ONE exception: `bench/scripts/` IS tracked. Harnesses there are
# hand-authored source that would otherwise exist in exactly one copy, in a
# tier nothing ever purges; a stray `rm -rf` loses work no backup, review or CI
# ever saw. The directory is empty today; un-ignoring it now means the first
# harness written here is tracked by default instead of silently unbacked.
# Build output and captures produced inside a harness dir stay ignored.
# (`/dir/*` + `!/dir/sub/` so a subdir can be re-included.)
/dev-docs/*
!/dev-docs/bench/
/dev-docs/bench/*
!/dev-docs/bench/scripts/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/target/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/__pycache__/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/node_modules/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.kgl
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.kgle
/inbox/

# macOS
.DS_Store
/.cargo/
